==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewbʰ- (cut off)}}
{{etymon|en|id=cabin|:inh|enm:logge<id:hut>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|logge|id=hut}}, from {{der|en|fro|loge|t=an arbour, a covered walk-way|id=hut}}.

See also {{cog|la-med|lobia}}, {{m|la|laubia}}; also {{cog|goh|louba|t=a porch, a gallery}} ({{cog|de|Laube|t=bower, arbor}}), {{cog|goh|loub|t=leaf, foliage}}, {{cog|ang|lēaf|t=leaf, foliage}}. {{doublet|en|loggia|lobby}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/lɒd͡ʒ/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/lɑd͡ʒ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-lodge.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒdʒ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[building]] for [[recreational]] [[use]] such as a [[hunting lodge]] or a [[summer]] [[cabin]].
# {{ellipsis of|en|porter's lodge}}: a [[building]] or [[room]] near the [[entrance]] of an [[estate]] or [[building]], [[especially]] {{lb|en|UK|Canada}} as a [[college]] [[mailroom]].
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|page=39|passage=[H]e walked across Hawthorn Tree Court on his way to the [[porter's lodge]]. {{...}} At the '''lodge''' he cleared his [[pigeon-hole]].}}
# A local chapter of some [[fraternity|fraternities]], such as [[freemason|freemasons]].
# {{lb|en|US}} A local chapter of a [[trade union]].
# A [[rural]] hotel or resort, an [[inn]].
# A [[beaver|beaver's]] shelter constructed on a pond or lake.
# A [[den]] or [[cave]].
# The [[chamber]] of an [[abbot]], [[prior]], or [[head]] of a [[college]].
# {{lb|en|mining}} The space at the mouth of a level next to the shaft, widened to permit wagons to pass, or ore to be deposited for hoisting; called also [[platt]].<ref>{{R:Raymond Glossary}}</ref>
# A collection of objects lodged together.
#* {{RQ:Defoe Captain Singleton|passage=the Maldives, a famous '''lodge''' of islands}}
# A [[Native American]] [[home]], such as [[teepee]] or [[wigwam]].
#* {{quote-book|en |author={{w|Dorothy M. Johnson}}|year=1950|newversion=in |type2=book |editor2=|title=Flame on the Frontier|title2=Indian Country|location2=London |publisher2=Corgi|year2=1961 |page2=28|text="In my '''lodge''' there is only one woman."}}
## {{lb|en|by extension}} The people who live in one such home; a [[household]].
## {{lb|en|historic}} A family of [[Native American]]s, or the persons who usually occupy an Indian lodge; as a unit of enumeration, reckoned from four to six persons.
##: {{ux|en|The tribe consists of about two hundred '''lodges''', that is, of about a thousand individuals.}}

